\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{e8b15c7}
\import{base-macros}

\p{One command runs the gate of a switch set and writes a report of one page: a differential run per declaration against the reference engine, tier equivalence with the generic tier (outcome and reason of every declaration, values of the code tier's judgments), convention equivalence (host depth 0 and unbounded against 128: outcome, ticks, call trace and every record, run and pair word), the audits, and the real pipeline on the 230 tests and four corpora. A second command runs the mutant corpora through the real driver with the machine as engine. The full gates of the generic tier and of \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} passed.}

\p{The gate found one convention difference, M8-F1: with \code{\verb~|gated~} and the code tier, two declarations of the Cedar slice took one tick more under host depth 0. A closed value that arrived through a frame did not fill the inline cache of its site, so the site evaluated the term again. The fix fills the cache at the resume, and the unit takes 53,059 ticks under both conventions (\commit{dcccdad}).}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M8.md}, \src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md}. Commit \commit{e8b15c7}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [the gate](design-gate).}
